    "title": "Veteran firefighter retiring after 36 years of dedicated service - NewsBreak",
    "text": "9 hours ago After providing more than 36 years of service to the communities of Salisbury, Statesville and Troutman, Jeff Leaptrott has decided to hang up his turnout gear for good. Leaptrott was hired by the Statesville Fire Department in May of 1990 after serving with the Salisbury Fire Department. He was promoted to the rank of captain in 1995 and the rank of battalion chief in April of 2008, before retiring from the SFD in July of 2016. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 8",
